          },
          "blocks": {
            "accordion_row_tF8heA": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Do you color match?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_BYQMeG": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Since most of our clients are seasoned printers, standard protocol usually involves no color matching on full-color printing as its mostly standard practice on single spot color images utilizing Pantone colors that are hand mixed. </p><p>We do have color charts we can provide if you wish to meet certain clients' needs. When it comes to standard CMYK printing, we are extremely confident in the colors our printers hit. At the same time, we do have a high standard and will always address issues if one arises.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": true,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 20,
                    "padding-block-start": 15,
                    "padding-block-end": 15,
                    "padding-inline-start": 15,
                    "padding-inline-end": 15
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_BYQMeG"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_7rmrdE": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Do you automatically fix artwork that I upload?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_HN9dJT": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Because we cater to professionals who print shirts for a living, the standard protocol is not to change anything without consent. With our gangsheet builder, we do provide the tools to erase backgrounds, halftone, or clean up semi-transparent pixels, which are usually 99% of any printing issues when it comes to DTF. If you wish for us to take a courtesy quality check, we would love to do so. If there are issues and we are given consent to make changes, we would not mind doing so. Just know that artwork changes may result in a change of turnaround time.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": true,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 20,
                    "padding-block-start": 15,
                    "padding-block-end": 15,
                    "padding-inline-start": 15,
                    "padding-inline-end": 15
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_HN9dJT"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_TNAeEi": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Do you accept AI created artwork?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_fgEKHi": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes, but it has its limits. Uploading original high-res logos or supporting high-res art will let you produce a print-ready 300dpi image. Using AI to generate images usually have a max resolution of 5-6 inches that scales at 300dpi. Use prompts with specific subject details, art style, aspect ratio, and technical keywords like \"ultra-detailed,\" and \"print-ready,\" often using a 1:1 or 2:3 ratio or specific inches. You will still have to upscale using an upscaling program or clean up semi-transparent pixels.<br/></p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": true,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 20,
                    "padding-block-start": 15,
                    "padding-block-end": 15,
                    "padding-inline-start": 15,
                    "padding-inline-end": 15
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_fgEKHi"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_zUJmEE": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What is the best way to prepare my gangsheet?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_VcBzgM": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Create a new 22-inch canvas, CMYK Mode, 300 dpi with transparent background and drag all artwork into that canvas. Based on the available template sizes, expand your way down to the size that best accommodates your artwork needs. Our preference is to save your art in PNG format. PNG supports transparent backgrounds and preserves detail/color.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": true,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 20,
                    "padding-block-start": 15,
                    "padding-block-end": 15,
                    "padding-inline-start": 15,
                    "padding-inline-end": 15
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_VcBzgM"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_mLhKwG": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Do you offer pre-cut transfers by size?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_MTB3TE": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>At this moment its not something we offer as we mostly cater to print brokers who order in gang sheets, opposed to single designs. While it's an option for the future, we wish to provide products that give you the best bang for your buck.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": true,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 20,
                    "padding-block-start": 15,
                    "padding-block-end": 15,
                    "padding-inline-start": 15,
                    "padding-inline-end": 15
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_MTB3TE"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_cEH4R4": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Do you prefer I use your gang sheet builder or upload one I made on my own?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_G6Ey6g": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>The honest truth is, if you can build it yourself, upload your own gang sheet, but please keep art sizes to their defined sizes. Our builder has great tools, but if you have big gaps of transparency in your artwork where you can possibly sneak something small in the gaps, that would be our preference, as you get more bang for your buck. Art pieces submitted on our builder recognize areas as square areas, and if you wish to overlap designs, you will get warnings and may have overlooked areas you didn't intend to overlap.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": true,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 20,
                    "padding-block-start": 15,
                    "padding-block-end": 15,
                    "padding-inline-start": 15,
                    "padding-inline-end": 15
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_G6Ey6g"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_CxQwtE": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What size should my halftones be?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_jMQz6Q": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Our best recommendation would be to use 30 lpi at 300dpi at 22.5 degree angle to keep at screen printing standards. Do not change the image size after you have halftoned your image as there will be unexpected results.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": true,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 20,
                    "padding-block-start": 15,
                    "padding-block-end": 15,
                    "padding-inline-start": 15,
                    "padding-inline-end": 15
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_jMQz6Q"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_JyqirN": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Your gang builder says I have semi-transparent pixels but its originally a vector art. Should I have your builder fix the issue?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_CMDPtA": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Our builder is very sensitive in that it recognizes anti-aliasing at very small levels. It should be fine to ignore any warnings as long as you didn't enlarge from a very small image to a much larger image.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
